=== plain-80: width 80, height 24, profile notty, dark, glyphs ascii, plain
# play environment/ubuntu2604 ----------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Play mode, mocks: the Environment screen proposed for slice 9,$
# drawn from what real code reads of a simulated host$
# (sudoers.Choose, Read, PlanFor), each change on the real$
# plan/apply engine (steps.Sudoers). Who ran hardn, the reader$
# of hardn's files and the plan's findings on the change are the$
# gallery's, unit (b)'s to build. Nothing on this machine$
# changes: every command and file is the fake's, and its record$
# is shown when play ends.$
$
# Info: environment/ubuntu2604$
# web-01.example.net runs Ubuntu 26.04, sudo-rs 0.2.13. alice$
# ran sudo hardn; sudo dropped HARDN_CONFIG.$
$
# Environment Variable Settings ################################$
$
# HARDN_CONFIG -------------------------------------------------$
$
   -  User                 alice$
  [ ] Under sudo           Not kept$
   -  Value                Not set$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Under sudo           Keep HARDN_CONFIG$
   2) Guide                How to set HARDN_CONFIG$
$
   0) Return$
$
  > Enter selection [0-2 or q]: 1$
$
# Keep HARDN_CONFIG ############################################$
$
# HARDN_CONFIG -------------------------------------------------$
$
   -  User                 alice$
  [+] Under sudo           Kept$
$
   -  Keep HARDN_CONFIG$
      /etc/sudoers.d/hardn-env-alice$
      @@ -0,0 +1,2 @@$
      +# Managed by hardn$
      +Defaults:alice env_keep += "HARDN_CONFIG"$
$
  Keep HARDN_CONFIG under sudo? [y/N, 0 or q]: y$
$
  [+] Keep HARDN_CONFIG    Done$
$
# Operation Successful$
$
  Takes effect at the next sudo hardn.$
$
# Environment Variable Settings ################################$
$
# HARDN_CONFIG -------------------------------------------------$
$
   -  User                 alice$
  [+] Under sudo           Kept$
   -  Value                Not set$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Under sudo           Stop keeping HARDN_CONFIG$
   2) Guide                How to set HARDN_CONFIG$
$
   0) Return$
$
  > Enter selection [0-2 or q]: 0$
$
# simulated system ---------------------------------------------$
$
# Info: environment/ubuntu2604$
# Recorded by the fake, not done: what each step ran on web-$
# 01.example.net, and the files it changed, in order; hardn's$
# own journal, run directory and backups left out.$
$
   -  Applied: Keep HARDN_CONFIG$
      /etc/sudoers.d/hardn-env-alice$
$

